ci(471,480,'stated without proof','E','The countable sum/product/inverse-limit assertions hold with the Hausdorff Lusin convention; the inverse-limit proof uses closed diagonals.', ['BourbakiTopology2007'],19,search=[12,13,14,15])
ci(472,481,'stated without proof','E','The strong-topology distribution assertion matches the checked specific example in Bourbaki, III§6 no2. No unrestricted theorem about all Fréchet duals is claimed.', ['BourbakiTVS1987'],19,search=[12,14,15],date='Checked English edition 1987; exact earlier French circulation not established')

# Codex B15-01 mathematical pages not receiving NOTES_INDEX rows.
c(473,[],[59],'B15-01:7–25','foncteurs ... admissibles ... équivalente',
 'For an A-linear category with the stated strict generator X and finite-projective tensor description, admissible A-linear functors to C′ are equivalent to O=End(X)-objects X′ for which the required P⊗_O X′ exist. Natural transformations are determined on X. In the Deuring rank-one case the allowed P are locally free of rank one over Spec(A).',
 'stated without proof','E','The strict-generator case follows from projective-module tensor/Hom duality and idempotent summands. The target tensor-existence condition is essential.', ['StacksKaroubi2026','StacksProjective2026','StacksDescent2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35],confidence='high')
c(474,[],[59],'B15-01:27–35','foncteur pleinement fidèle canonique',
 'Yoneda gives a fully faithful A-linear functor X↦Hom_C(-,X) into the indicated coadmissible functor category, with representable functors preserving the relevant existing limits/Hom operations.',
 'stated without proof','E','The ordinary enriched Yoneda argument verifies full faithfulness. It does not assert that every coadmissible functor is representable.', ['StacksYoneda2026','StacksDescent2026','StacksProjective2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])
c(475,[],[61,63],'Pro15_034-086:481–507; B15-01:56','raisonnables ... stricts ... pleinement fidèle',
 'With the reasonable-product definition on Pro61 and strict generator X, the category is equivalent to its full image in finite projective right End(X)-modules, containing the regular module. The projective tensor/Hom identification gives the Hom comparison.',
 'proof sketched','E','The boundary is resolved by reading Pro61 together with Codex63. The proof via corner matrices is supplied in P15; no absent definition is posited.', ['StacksKaroubi2026','StacksProjective2026','StacksDescent2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])
c(476,[],[63],'B15-01:56–68','et inversement? ... limite inductive',
 'The sheet asks for a converse and asserts that a jolie category is a filtered union of full strictly monogenic subcategories. Directedness requires a common strict generator for every finite collection, for example from appropriate finite direct sums; the preceding definition alone does not explicitly supply it.',
 'open on the pages','F','The strict-generator Morita statement is clear, but the exact weaker jolie axioms needed for the filtered-union equivalence remain underdetermined. A modern theorem cannot silently add additivity.', ['StacksKaroubi2026','StacksProjective2026','StacksDescent2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35],confidence='medium')
c(477,[],[81],'B15-01:85–89','Elle n’est pratiquement jamais un champ',
 'The same-object category with Hom⊗_A A′ is a fibre category on affine A-schemes; it need not satisfy effective descent on the big Zariski site. Localizability is defined as the stack condition on the small affine Zariski site of Spec(A).',
 'stated without proof','E','The failure is explained by descent of a nontrivial projective module absent from the free same-object category. The word practically is informal; no assertion of failure for every C is extracted.', ['StacksYoneda2026','StacksDescent2026','StacksProjective2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])
c(478,[],[81],'B15-01:92–98','localement isomorphes à X',
 'If C is localizable over A, R acts on X, and P is a right R-module locally isomorphic to R over Spec(A), then P⊗_R X exists by descent. If R→End_C(X) is an isomorphism, this functor is fully faithful with image the objects locally isomorphic to X.',
 'stated without proof','E','Local trivializations and transition matrices prove the assertion, with the specified site and endomorphism-algebra condition.', ['StacksKaroubi2026','StacksProjective2026','StacksDescent2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])
c(479,[],[81,82],'B15-01:100–109','additive ... karoubienne',
 'For additive localizable C, the same result holds for finite locally free R-modules, with objects locally isomorphic to finite sums of X. For additive Karoubian C and R=End(X), finite projective right R-modules give the full subcategory of summands of finite sums of X without a localization hypothesis.',
 'stated without proof','E','The local statement follows by descent; the projective statement is independently proved by splitting idempotents.', ['StacksKaroubi2026','StacksProjective2026','StacksDescent2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])
c(480,[],[82],'B15-01:111–121','c’est donc un champ',
 'For the stated finite-type A-algebra R, objects of C with R action form an A-linear category whose small-Spec(A) localization is a stack whenever C is. Endomorphisms giving the action and all algebra relations descend with the object.',
 'proof sketched','E','The assertion holds on the explicitly specified base site. The transcribed objects of R should be checked against objects of C as a type alarm.', ['StacksYoneda2026','StacksDescent2026','StacksProjective2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])
c(481,[],[82],'B15-01:123–125','Notre raisonnement ne prouve pas',
 'For commutative R, R-linearity of Mod(R,C) does not by this argument establish localizability on Spec(R). Restriction of a localizable category to an affine open of Spec(A) is localizable and gives the restricted stack.',
 'open on the pages','F','The restriction statement is formal; the stronger Spec(R) assertion needs additional hypotheses not stated here. The manuscript accurately marks the gap.', ['StacksYoneda2026','StacksDescent2026','StacksProjective2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35],confidence='medium')
c(482,[],[82],'B15-01:127','apparentés ... catégorie de Deuring',
 'Local isomorphism over Spec(A) is an equivalence relation. The full subcategory of objects locally isomorphic to a given X is localizable and is the associated Deuring category in the source’s terminology.',
 'stated without proof','E','Descent of isomorphisms and the rank-one module description establish the precise assertion.', ['StacksKaroubi2026','StacksProjective2026','StacksDescent2026'],15,search=[26,28,29,30,34,35])

# Reused analytic manuscript: each assertion searched; provenance remains separate.
def an(n,sc,ln,words,stmt,status='proved there',cl='E',fate='The precise local analytic statement is established; the supplied fragment was checked directly.',proof=16,blocks=(),refs=None,search=None):
    c(n,[],sc,ln,words,stmt,status,cl,fate,refs or ['BourbakiVarietes1967'],proof,blocks,search or [9,10,12,13,14,15,16],date='Classical analytic result; checked Bourbaki fascicles 1967/1971, exact recycled draft unidentified')
an(483,[62],'B15-01:40–46','prolongement analytique', 'For Banach-valued real or complex analytic functions on a family of domains with each nonempty pairwise overlap connected, equality on a nonempty open subset of each overlap gives a unique glued analytic function on the union.')
an(484,[62],'B15-01:48–52','Zorn ... unique', 'Every analytic function on a connected real/complex domain has a maximal single-valued extension to some containing domain by Zorn. On a fixed connected maximal domain the extension is unique; different maximal domains need not coincide.')
an(485,[64],'B15-01:77–79','variété linéaire réelle', 'Complex holomorphic functions agreeing on a relatively open full-dimensional totally real affine slice agree near that slice and hence on the connected overlap. In one real/complex variable, an accumulating zero set with an interior accumulation point gives the same conclusion.')
an(486,[64],'B15-01:75','dans H ... dans H', 'Two square-root branches can agree on one component of a disconnected overlap and be negatives on the other. The second H in the last sentence must designate the other component H′ for the displayed angles to be consistent.',status='false as stated',fate='The example is valid with its two components distinguished. This is a frozen label alarm, not an unqualified failure of analytic uniqueness.')
an(487,[27,29,31],'B15-02:6–8;17–40','expression différentielle fermée', 'On a simply connected domain in R^n or C^n, a closed analytic one-form with Banach-space coefficients has a global analytic primitive, unique up to a constant. Its integral is invariant under endpoint-fixed homotopy and vanishes on null-homotopic loops. The word contractile is defined here only by triviality of loops.',refs=['BourbakiVarietes1967','Cristoferi2016'],search=[9,10,14,15,22,23])
an(488,[31],'B15-02:42','continument différentiables ... vaut la peine?', 'The Cauchy/homotopy assertion extends to closed C¹ real one-forms on simply connected open domains; the primitive is C² for C¹ coefficients.',status='open on the pages',fate='The extension is established by the same local-primitive and homotopy argument. The remaining manuscript question is editorial usefulness, not an unsolved mathematical theorem.',refs=['Cristoferi2016','BourbakiVarietes1967'],search=[22,23])
an(489,[29,35],'B15-02:23–25;64–72','relation d’équivalence ... linéaire par morceaux', 'Homotopy of paths with fixed parameter interval is an equivalence relation. Star-shaped domains admit the displayed contraction. Any path in an open real/complex domain can be deformed with fixed endpoints to a polygonal path; any two points of a connected open domain are polygonally connected. Concatenating independently chosen free homotopies requires compatible junctions.')
an(490,[27],'B15-02:10–12','principe général ... enfin, si', 'A proposed abstract analytic-continuation principle lists local existence/uniqueness conditions and then breaks off before its final hypothesis. The preceding primitive theorem does not identify the complete intended statement.',status='stated without proof',cl='F',fate='The exact continuation principle is not identifiable from the incomplete paragraph. The ordinary monodromy/primitive result is separately checked in C-SA06-487.')
an(491,[33],'B15-02:52–59','t_{alpha+1}-t', 'The polygonal interpolation formula requires denominator t_{alpha+1}-t_alpha. The literal variable denominator develops a pole at the right endpoint except in the constant case.',status='false as stated',fate='Exact endpoint substitution detects the index alarm; the homotopy proof works with ordinary affine interpolation.',blocks=['analytic_interpolation'])
an(492,[37],'B15-02:87–91','P∩Q ... tout x', 'Two Banach-valued analytic power series on intersecting real/complex polycylinders agree on the whole intersection if they agree on a nonempty open subset. The intersection is convex and line restriction reduces the proof to one variable.')
an(493,[39],'B15-02:95–132','conditions (20)', 'For ∂_i y_j=U_{ij}(x,y), analytic Frobenius compatibility is ∂_k U_{ij}+Σ_h∂_{y_h}U_{ij}U_{kh}=∂_i U_{kj}+Σ_h∂_{y_h}U_{kj}U_{ih}. The printed last U_{jh} is incompatible with the chain rule. With correct compatibility, local analytic solutions follow from commuting flows/radial ODE integration.',status='false as stated',fate='The theorem with the correct chain-rule index is established. The system U11=y,U21=2y has correct bracket zero but fails the printed formula, providing an exact diagnostic.',proof=18,blocks=['Frobenius_index'])
an(494,[41],'B15-02:133–147','isomorphisme ... réciproque', 'Local analytic flow maps are invertible by reversing time and satisfy the flow composition law wherever the relevant germs are defined, by uniqueness of the initial-value problem.',proof=18)
an(495,[43,45,47],'B15-02:148–197;215','h_i ... produit ... h_i', 'Analytic ODEs over a complete valued field of characteristic zero have local solutions with the stated analytic parameters and initial data. Coefficient recursion uses products of h_j matching each substituted dependent variable and complete parameter multiindices; the printed h_i throughout the product is wrong.',status='false as stated',fate='The local germ theorem is established; the vector coefficient formula needs the displayed index repair. It does not assert uniqueness on arbitrary disconnected ultrametric domains.',proof=18,blocks=['ODE_component_index'])
an(496,[47,49],'B15-02:202; B15-03:5–34','différentielle ... inversible', 'An analytic map of finite-dimensional spaces over a complete valued field with invertible derivative has an analytic inverse on suitable neighbourhoods; the corresponding implicit equation has a unique local solution germ. The source’s majorant argument controls the local radius.',proof=17,refs=['BourbakiVarietes1967','Glockner2003'])
an(497,[47],'B15-02:209','x^n ... n assez grand', 'A real analytic function with nowhere-zero derivative on an interval is strictly monotone and globally invertible onto its image. In contrast, z↦z^13 has nonzero derivative on |z-1|<1/2 but is not injective there.',proof=18,blocks=['complex_inverse_warning'])
an(498,[47],'B15-02:211','dépendance ... jacobien identiquement nul', 'The requested dependence theorem needs a constant-rank or other precise hypothesis. The arbitrary-germ implication from identically zero Jacobian to an analytic relation is false: (u,v,w)↦(u,uv,uv exp(v)) has generic rank2 but no nonzero formal or analytic relation among its components at0.',status='open on the pages',cl='C',fate='The constant-rank statement is established; Osgood’s classical example refutes the strongest unrestricted germ reading. The fragment does not say which quantifiers were intended.',proof=18,blocks=['Osgood'],refs=['BelottoCurmiRond2021','Osgood1916','BourbakiVarietes1967'],search=[16,17,18,19,20])
an(499,[49],'B15-03:5–19','(1-q mu v)(1+qM mu)v', 'The symmetric majorant system forces all v_i equal; its zero-constant scalar solution is the displayed quadratic radical branch. Absolute convergence follows near0 after the radicand is near1.',proof=17,blocks=['analytic_majorant'])
an(500,[49],'B15-03:21;29–34','binom(1/2,n)v^n; u_i≤|=w_i', 'The correct binomial series is Σ binom(1/2,n)(-w)^n. The uniqueness statement is equality u_i=w_i and the difference bound involves u_k-w_k, not a separate v_k. The literal alternatives are mathematical alarms.',status='false as stated',fate='The quadratic solution and contraction uniqueness survive these repairs; no reading is chosen without a scan.',proof=17,blocks=['analytic_majorant'])
an(501,[53,51],'B15-03:76–82;39–60','pour tout couple de points', 'Analytic functions satisfy strict differentiability: uniformly for u,v sufficiently close to a, ||f(u)-f(v)-Df(a)(u-v)||≤epsilon max|u_k-v_k|. Termwise analytic derivatives then give indefinite differentiability.',proof=17,refs=['BourbakiVarietes1967','Glockner2003'])
an(502,[51],'B15-03:45–52','≤ M t² Σ', 'With M=sup ||b_nm||r^(|n|+|m|), extracting t² from terms |m|≥2 requires M r^(-2)t². The printed estimate omits r^(-2), and a scalar quadratic remainder refutes it.',status='false as stated',fate='The estimate is false with the printed definition of M; the corrected bound proves the intended strict differentiability result.',proof=17,blocks=['analytic_remainder'])
an(503,[53],'B15-03:67–73','|1/n|≤n^beta', 'For a complete valued field of characteristic0, the restriction of its absolute value to Q gives |1/n|≤n^beta for a fixed beta. Coefficient division for a closed analytic form therefore preserves convergence on every strictly smaller polyradius, producing a local analytic primitive.',proof=17,refs=['BourbakiVarietes1967','MilneANT2020'],search=[9,10,12,13,14,15,16,37])
an(504,[53],'B15-03:69–73','converge en même temps', 'Multiplying convergent boundary terms by polynomial weights need not preserve convergence at that same radius. At r=1, a_n=(n+1)^(-2) is summable while (n+1)a_n is not. The valid assertion is equality of open convergence domains, or convergence after shrinking radii.',status='false as stated',fate='The boundary statement is false literally; the germ-level analytic conclusion remains valid.',proof=17,blocks=['analytic_radius'])
an(505,[51],'B15-03:54–62','zéro d’ordre h ... caractéristique0', 'An analytic function is indefinitely differentiable. In one variable its order of zero is the first nonzero Taylor exponent; in characteristic0 this agrees with the first nonzero derivative order. The final sentence on this sheet is incomplete, so no further formula is supplied.',proof=17)
an(506,[55],'B15-03:89–93','fonction composée ... holomorphe', 'Composition of analytic functions with the stated scalar inner map and Banach-valued outer function is analytic wherever the image lies in its domain, by absolute substitution.',proof=17)
an(507,[55],'B15-03:95–97','multilinéaire continue', 'A continuous multilinear map on Banach spaces carries tuples of analytic functions to an analytic function. The proof uses its norm-product bound and absolute summability of the product coefficient family.',proof=17)
an(508,[55],'B15-03:99','chacune des fonctions scalaires', 'A finite vector-valued function is analytic iff all scalar coordinate functions are analytic, since finite products preserve the relevant local convergent power-series expansions.',proof=17)
an(509,[57],'B15-03:110–120','r_k-|a_k|', 'A power series absolutely convergent on a polydisk of radii r_k re-expands around a point a on |u_k|<r_k-|a_k|. Its sum is analytic in that polydisk, with the given local-power-series definition.',proof=17)
an(510,[57],'B15-03:104','associativité', 'Successive substitutions of absolutely convergent power series are associative on neighbourhoods where the stated majorant/substitutability conditions hold. The fragment is the conclusion of that theorem, not an unconditional formal rearrangement of divergent series.',proof=17)

# Additional assertions discovered in text rather than indexed headings.
c(511,[],[90,92],'Pro61–62;94–98','x^{i/nu}',
 'The compactness proof should use |x|^(i/nu) for x∈R*. Writing a fractional power of a possibly negative real x is not generally defined. Raising to a further even power or retaining absolute values resolves the proof.',
 'false as stated','E','This is a local notation alarm; the spectral-modulus result C-SA06-402 is valid.', ['MilneCM2020','DeligneMilne1982'],1,['weight_and_sign'],[1,3,16,21])
c(512,[405,406,407],[98,100],'Pro221–225;252–258;274','λ∈K; λ²=q^{i/2}u; poids ... mi′',
 'Three distinct literal alarms: the CM element should range in L for the subsequent L-divisor argument; λ²=q^{i/2}u has modulus q^{i/4} when |u|=1; and a fixed eigenvalue of weights i,i′ relative to p^n,p^m obeys ni=mi′. These are not new conjectures.',
 'false as stated','E','Exact norm/modulus tests locate each discrepancy. Actual finite-field extension raises the eigenvalue and preserves its cohomological weight, a different operation from changing the base attached to a fixed number.', ['MilneCM2020','TateHonda1968'],2,['weight_and_sign'],[1,16,17,21])
c(513,[],[103],'Pro347–360','homomorphismes ... isomorphisme',
 'Pushforward along a ringed-space morphism has natural internal-Hom and tensor comparison maps; pullback is extension of scalars and has a natural tensor isomorphism. The unit and counit have the stated domains once the missing source of rho_A is supplied.',
 'stated without proof','E','These canonical constructions are checked sectionwise in P14 and match the ringed-space formalism; the separate adjunction subscript alarm is C-SA06-469.', ['StacksRinged2026'],14,search=[22,23,24])
c(514,[],[121],'Pro742;758','Un autom ... qui respecte i est l’identité',
 'For a Q-torus whose rational cocharacter space is generated by the Galois conjugates of i, a Q-automorphism fixing i fixes every conjugate and is the identity. Over R or C, or without the spanning hypothesis, this conclusion does not follow.',
 'stated without proof','E','The exact rational spanning version is a linear-algebra argument. It is separate from the unresolved polarization-orbit question.', ['MilneCM2020','MilneFiniteFields1994'],10,['CM23'],[5,6,8,16,21])

